# Migrations are checksummed, so their bytes must not depend on the machine.
#
# core.autocrlf=true hands out CRLF on Windows while git stores LF. A migration
# checked out on such a PC hashes differently from the one that ran, and the
# append-only guard then refuses to start: "0006 has changed since it was
# applied". Nothing had changed - only the line endings.
#
# The checksum is a property of the migration, not of who checked it out.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read as bytes by the installer and the bundler.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
